# Guest-side assets are byte-for-byte artifacts: they get copied into a
# Windows image, so git must never normalise their line endings.
#
# The .cmd files are deliberately mixed -- 3 are CRLF, 9 are LF, and both work
# under cmd.exe. The risk is not the mix, it is silent conversion: a Python
# rewrite of bvgpu-firstboot.cmd turned its CRLF into LF, which no editor and
# no `git diff --stat` showed, and buried a 27-line change in a 269-line
# whole-file rewrite. -text pins whatever each file already is.
scripts/win-assets/** -text whitespace=cr-at-eol
scripts/patches/virtio-win-mesa-submit-trace.patch text eol=lf whitespace=-blank-at-eol
